# Send to md1

When the user says **"отправь в md1"**, **"send to md1"**, **"save to md1"**, **"share this doc"**, **"дай ссылку на док"**, or similar:

1. Use the **md1** MCP server tools (requires `MD1_API_TOKEN` in MCP config).
2. For a **file path** → `md1_create_from_file` with that path.
3. For **inline content** or a selection → `md1_create_doc` with the markdown body.
4. When the user wants a **link to send to others** → pass `share: true` on create, or call `md1_share_doc` for an existing note.
5. To **read** a note first → `md1_get_doc` with id, slug, or part of the title.
6. Infer title from the first `# heading` or the filename unless the user gave a title.
7. Reply with the **Share link** (`https://md1.space/d/…`) prominently when published; editor URL is secondary.

If MCP tools are unavailable, tell the user to:
- Create an API token at https://md1.space/settings (works with curl/any HTTP client too)
- Configure the md1 MCP server from `mcp.json.example` and [docs/API.md](docs/API.md)
- Restart the MCP host after config changes
